<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#calligraphy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calligraphy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calligraphy is the art of decorative handwriting, highly developed in the Islamic world, where it adorned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, buildings and objects. Persian calligraphy, especially the nastaliq script, was a prestigious art at Iranian courts. It formed part of the cultural patronage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a>.</p></div>
